# VVDN -- 5 DEPARTURES TAXI-OUT TO RWY 35R (ADDWPT/LNAV version).
# Callsigns VDN801-805 are SYNTHETIC. Real data: apt.dat 1300 parking rows
# (Gate 36/32/4/5/6 -- Gate 24-28 substituted per earlier discussion, being
# graph-disconnected in every real dataset checked) + real 1201/1202
# taxi-route nodes from each gate to the RWY 35R hold point (node 41),
# found via Dijkstra over the real graph.
#
# DEP_HOLD updated to the user-specified 16.0292,108.2025, nose on 352
# (real runway heading). The real node41 -> DEP_HOLD hop is only ~2m --
# too short for LNAV's turn anticipation to settle cleanly onto 352 -- so
# one synthetic point, FINAL_APPROACH, sits ~80m short of DEP_HOLD exactly
# on the 352-degree bearing (not a real apt.dat node; a geometric
# construction purely to give LNAV a real final leg to align the heading
# on before the short last hop into the exact hold coordinate).
#
# Uses ADDWPT + LNAV/VNAV, not MOVE: this scenario has no cross-aircraft
# coordination (no hold-indefinitely-for-another-aircraft's-trigger, no
# pushback-reverse modeling) -- the one thing MOVE is actually needed for
# elsewhere in this project (see VVDN_35L35R_COORDINATED_OPS.scn's header
# and VVDN_1HR_MULTI_GATE_DEP_35R.scn's, the latter also documenting a
# confirmed BlueSky engine instability below 4kt that ADDWPT sidesteps
# simply by never commanding anything that slow). Matches this project's
# existing ADDWPT-based taxi convention (VVNB_TAXI_DEP_60min.scn etc.):
# alt=0ft, spd=15kt per taxi waypoint, spd=25kt at the final "ready for
# departure" waypoint.
00:00:00.00>TRAILS ON
00:00:00.00>ASAS OFF

# ---- VDN801 (Gate 36, real apt.dat route) ----
00:00:00.00>CRE VDN801 B738 16.048686 108.201668 172.1 0 15
00:00:00.00>VDN801 ADDWPT 16.048253,108.201906 0 15
